WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.329
The inverse matrix. In this lesson you will

2
00:00:03.329 --> 00:00:06.580
learn how to find the inverse of a matrix.

3
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.540
What is an inverse matrix? Here we can draw an
analogy with reciprocal numbers.

4
00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.954
Every number a has a reciprocal,

5
00:00:14.954 --> 00:00:19.220
a to the power minus one, and the product of
these numbers

6
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:23.920
equals one. A similar notion is introduced for
square matrices.

7
00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:31.480
First, let us introduce some key notions. If
the determinant of a square matrix

8
00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.756
is zero, the matrix is called singular;

9
00:00:34.756 --> 00:00:39.040
if it is nonzero, the matrix is called
nonsingular.

10
00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:47.860
The matrix A to the power minus one is called
the inverse of A

11
